                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 21.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Mason to Earl Russell.—Russell.—(Received October 2)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-09-28"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 28, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Mason presents his compliments to Earl Russell, and has the honor to enclose
                    herewith two original papers pertaining to the case of the Margaret and Jessie,
                    recently received from the parties interested.</p>
                <p>Mr. Mason does this because of his previous knowledge that this case had been
                    brought to the notice of Earl Russell.</p>



                <xi:include href="d379-a1.xml" xpointer="d379-a1"/>
            </div>
